The admins here at the UW have cooked up a semi-quota system for mail
owing to the fact that some people were using their mailboxes as extra
storage, causing the mail spooling area to fill up rapidly and often.
Mail now counts against quota, and if mail is received while a user is
over quota it goes to a special "redelivery" area, and the user cannot
receive that mail until they get their quota back down.

It still has some problems and quirks, but you may be able to adapt their
solution to your problem.  I'm not sure who the best person to contact
about this would be, but some official account at cac.washington.edu 
would be a good starting point.  Please don't direct any queries about
the system to me, as I'm just a user.



