The affair involving the young man at the University of Illinois is not a
censorship issue. I believe I have made that plain, and if I have not,
please excuse my poor command of the English language.
The issue is more narrowly defined by 1) the concept of willful and
intentional infliction of emotional distress, 2) unlawful access to
stored communications, 3)dissemination of political propaganda in aid to
a foreign power, 4)use of public funds in support of the above activities.

Title 18 U.S.C. Sec. 2701 provides in part that any person who
intentionally accesses without authorization a facility through which an
electronic communication service is provided; or [and here is operative
language] intentionally exceeds an authorization to access that facility,
and thereby obtains or alters authorized access is in violation of
federal law and may be punished by a fine of $250,000. or imprisonment
for one year, or both.

The "Student Code" at an Illinois University may impress the students and
faculty. So will a full-blown federal investigation.

Were Mr. Kohr's activities confined to the posting of opinion, we could
ignore him or not as we might choose. Regretably, Mr. Kohr's activities
are not so confined (and I might add that his activities encompass not
only our own SCV, but the alt.war.vietnam newsgroup, where the American
veterans are less gentle with him than we are).

Mr. Kohr has publicly identified himself as a devotee of the VVAW
(Vietnam Veterans Against the War), an organization which itself has been
the subject of both a congressional investigation and a federal
investigation, centering on allegations that it functioned or functions
as a propaganda organ for the Communist Party of Vietnam, and indeed, Mr.
Kohr publicly claims to be an intimate associate of the Illinois
leadership of VVAW.

The VVAW, according to congressional investigators, has in the past
exhibited outlinks to Vietnamese Communist organizations in the Middle
West and elsewhere.

Those on SCV who are not aware of Mr. Kohr's self-admitted link to this
rather suspect organization might be tempted to think him an innocent, or
might be misled into thinking this is a free speech issue. This is not,
for the record now, a free speech issue.

There is a dark and bloody hand at work here...if you fail to recognize
it, ask someone who lived through the nightmare, or search your own memory.
The issue of whether or not Mr. Kohr is "witting" or a painfully
disturbed pawn awaits further examination. Those of you who are familiar
with Communist organizing tactics should be able to recognize the pattern.


-- 
